Two blocks slide directly towards each other along a frictionless horizontal surface, as shown in Fig. 4.1. The blocks collide and then move as shown in Fig. 4.2.

{{figure:figure_4_1.png}}

{{figure:figure_4_2.png}}

Block X initially moves to the right with a momentum of $0.37\,\mathrm{kg\,m\,s^{-1}}$. Block Y initially moves to the left with a momentum of $0.65\,\mathrm{kg\,m\,s^{-1}}$. After the blocks collide, block X moves to the left back along its original path with a momentum of $0.13\,\mathrm{kg\,m\,s^{-1}}$. Block Y also moves to the left after the collision.
